<title>HONG KONG: Orient Tel says year loss at HK$23 mln.</title>
<headline>Orient Tel says year loss at HK$23 mln.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-03-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended December 31</p>
<p>(in million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (H.K. cents)	   10.7 loss  vs 36.5 gain</p>
<p>    Dividend (H.K. cents)    nil	  vs nil</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	  10.33 loss vs 2.63 loss</p>
<p>    Net			    23.29 loss vs 76.41 profit</p>
<p>    Turnover		     669.50     vs 619.97</p>
<p>    Company name		 Orient Telecom &amp; Technology</p>
<p>				     Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close		  N/A</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	   N/A</p>
<p>NOTE - Orient Telecom &amp; Technology is involved in network telephone services in Bangkok, electricity generation in China's Shenyang, and development property in Hong Kong.</p>
<p>Net is after an exceptional loss mainly on provision for diminution in value of a long term investment.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6368</p>
</text>
